    title: "Term and Termination",
    slug: "section-vii",
    html: '<p class="pl-7 -indent-7"><span class="font-semibold">A.</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;Term. The term of this HIPAA Agreement shall commence as of the Effective Date, be coterminous with the Services Agreement, and continue in full force and effect from year to year, but shall terminate as of the earliest occurrence of any of the following:</p>\n<p class="ml-7 pl-7 -indent-7">(1)&nbsp;&nbsp;The Services Agreement is terminated; </p>\n<p class="ml-7 pl-7 -indent-7">(2)&nbsp;&nbsp;This HIPAA Agreement is terminated for cause as described in Section VII.B below;</p>\n<p class="ml-7 pl-7 -indent-7">(3)&nbsp;&nbsp;The parties mutually agree to terminate this HIPAA Agreement; or </p>\n<p class="ml-7 pl-7 -indent-7">(4)&nbsp;&nbsp;This HIPAA Agreement is terminated under applicable federal, state, or local law.</p>\n<p class="pl-7 -indent-7"><span class="font-semibold">B.</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;Termination for Cause. Upon Company\'s determination of a material breach by Business Associate of this HIPAA Agreement, Company shall notify Business Associate of its knowledge of such breach and shall have the right but not the duty to terminate this HIPAA Agreement and the Services Agreement after providing Business Associate with a 30-day period to cure the breach or end the violation, unless immediate termination is required by law. Such termination shall take effect within a reasonable period of time after written notice from Company to Business Associate that this HIPAA Agreement is being terminated, absent extraordinary circumstances; provided, however, that the obligations imposed on Business Associate pursuant to this HIPAA Agreement shall continue until the date when all PHI held by Business Associate is destroyed, returned to Company, or, if it is infeasible to return or destroy PHI, protections are extended to such information in accordance with Section VII.C below. In lieu of immediate termination, Company may, but does not have the duty to, provide Business Associate with an opportunity to cure the breach or end the violation within thirty (30) days.</p>\n<p class="pl-7 -indent-7"><span class="font-semibold">C.</span>&nbsp;&nbsp;Effect of Termination </p>\n<p class="ml-7 pl-7 -indent-7">(1)&nbsp;&nbsp;Upon termination of this HIPAA Agreement for any reason, Business Associate shall return or destroy all PHI that Business Associate still maintains in any form. Business Associate shall retain no copies of such PHI.</p>\n<p class="ml-7 pl-7 -indent-7">(2)&nbsp;&nbsp;If return or destruction of any or all PHI is not feasible, Business Associate shall:</p>\n<p class="ml-14 pl-7 -indent-7">(i)&nbsp;&nbsp;Notify Company of the conditions that make return or destruction of all PHI not feasible;</p>\n<p class="ml-14 pl-7 -indent-7">(ii)&nbsp;&nbsp;Retain only that PHI for which is necessary for Business Associate to continue its proper management and administration or to carry out its legal responsibilities;</p>\n<p class="ml-14 pl-7 -indent-7">(iii)&nbsp;&nbsp;Return to Company, or at Company’s direction, or destroy the remaining PHI that Business Associate still maintains in any form;</p>\n<p class="ml-14 pl-7 -indent-7">(iv)&nbsp;&nbsp;Extend the protections and obligations of this HIPAA Agreement to any retained PHI for as long as Business Associate retains the PHI;</p>\n<p class="ml-14 pl-7 -indent-7">(v)&nbsp;&nbsp;Not use or disclose the PHI retained by Business Associate other than for the purposes for which such PHI was retained and subject to the same conditions set forth in Sections IV.B and IV.C of this HIPAA Agreement that applied prior to termination; and</p>\n<p class="ml-14 pl-7 -indent-7">(vi)&nbsp;&nbsp;Return to Company or, at Company’s direction, destroy the PHI retained by Business Associate when it is no longer needed by Business Associate for its proper management and administration or to carry out its legal responsibilities.</p>\n<p class="ml-7 pl-7 -indent-7">(3)&nbsp;&nbsp;These provisions of this Section VII.C shall apply to PHI that is in the possession of Subcontractors or agents of Business Associate.</p>\n<p class="ml-7 pl-7 -indent-7">(4)&nbsp;&nbsp;Upon request by Company, Business Associate shall certify to Company that it has destroyed or returned all PHI.</p>\n<p class="ml-7 pl-7 -indent-7">(5)&nbsp;&nbsp;Any PHI that Business Associate destroys shall be destroyed in accordance with HIPAA.</p>',
